/target
# second-toolchain build dir: `--features dense` can't link on the default gnu toolchain here
# (getrandom 0.3 raw-dylib needs dlltool.exe), so dense/msvc builds go to an isolated target dir
# to keep the warm gnu cache untouched (`cargo clean` is forbidden). Never ship it — 756 MB.
/target-msvc
# same, for the dense-feature build (`--features dense` pulls model2vec + tokenizers, so it gets its
# own dir rather than thrashing the plain msvc cache). Multiple GB — never ship it.
/target-msvc-dense
# scratch/debug programs left at the repo root (not part of the build)
/test_*.rs
*.exe

# local code-review scratch (never ship)
.codex-review/

# runtime state dir (session slots, coordination locks, hostbot/persona/memory state) — never ship
.aizen/

# demo video is embedded via GitHub web upload (user-attachments URL), not tracked in the repo
dist/liveaizen.mp4

# review scratch: crystallized diffs handed to review subagents (regenerated per review)
.aizen-tmp/
.main_diff.txt
main_diff*.txt
